# Sign-in flow (Auth:Mode = Accounts), runnable from Visual Studio.
# Development runs with Auth:Mode = None until the UI has sign-in screens (roadmap 0.1d). To try these requests,
# set "Auth:Mode": "Accounts" in the API's user secrets and restart it.

@host = https://localhost:3001
@tab = http-file-tab

### Which screens the UI shows: mode (Accounts/None) and sign-up (Open/Closed)
GET {{host}}/api/auth/settings

### Create an account (passwords: at least 10 characters)
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "user@example.com", "password": "user-password-1" }

### Sign in. The browser uses ?useCookies=true and gets the session cookie; here useCookies=false returns a
### bearer token, which the requests below send.
# @name login
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login?useCookies=false
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "user@example.com", "password": "user-password-1" }

### Who am I
GET {{host}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Every API call needs sign-in plus the tab id header ("Not Connected" is expected: no connection yet)
GET {{host}}/api/databaseSchema/databases/not-connected
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
id: {{tab}}

### Without sign-in: 401
GET {{host}}/api/auth/me
